From: Filippo Falezza <filippo.falezza@outlook.com>
Date: Wed, 21 Oct 2026 19:38:57 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 145/159] ASoC: qcom: q6voice: Add codec DMA ports

On SoCs with the LPASS codec macros (SM8250, SM7250), the WCD938x
codec is reached through the RX_CODEC_DMA_RX_0 and TX_CODEC_DMA_TX_3
AFE ports, which the voice mixers did not offer.

Add an "RX_CODEC_DMA_RX_0 Voice Mixer" for the CS-VOICE and
VOICEMMODE1 downlinks, and TX_CODEC_DMA_TX_3 as an input of both
capture mixers.

This patch was generated by an AI coding assistant (Claude Opus 5.5 in
Claude Code) during an interactive bring-up session on a Motorola Moto G
5G Plus (XT2075-3, "nairo"). It has not yet been reviewed line by line
by a human and needs that review before any submission.

Assisted-by: LLM
Signed-off-by: Filippo Falezza <filippo.falezza@outlook.com>
---
